  "summary": "Removes legacy reverse-precedence handling in SettingsValue GetSetting, making later settings take precedence over earlier ones across all sources. This backward-compatibility quirk is rendered obsolete once prerequisite PR #17493 forbids multiple assignments to single-value settings in configuration files.",
  "problem": "Bitcoin Core's settings parser historically used reverse precedence for configuration files, where the first assigned value took priority over later values instead of standard last-wins precedence. This added complexity and special-casing to settings interpretation.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'This change implements one of the settings simplifications listed in #17508.'",
    "PR description: 'This has no effect on behavior because as of https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/17493 it's not possible to specify multiple values for single value settings in the config file.'"
